    <string name="help_activity_title">Help</string>
    <string name="help_text"><b>Geocache Placer</b> helps you find a precise GPS position for your geocache by averaging many measurements.\n\n<b>How to use the app:</b>\n\n<b>1. Wait for GPS signal</b>\nWhen the app opens, your current position (Pos) and satellite count (Sat) are shown. More satellites = better accuracy. Wait for at least 8–10.\n\n<b>2. Press Run</b>\nThe app starts measuring GPS positions. Each measurement appears as a red circle on the map.\n\n<b>3. Follow the results</b>\n• <b>Pos</b> — latest GPS measurement\n• <b>Avg</b> — average of all measurements (blue circle)\n• <b>Dev</b> — deviation between latest and previous average\n• <b>Count</b> — number of measurements taken\n• <b>Alt</b> — altitude above sea level\n• <b>Sat</b> — number of GPS satellites used\n\nWhen Dev is close to 0, the position is accurate.\n\n<b>4. Buttons</b>\n• <b>Run</b> — start/continue measuring\n• <b>Pause</b> — pause measurement\n• <b>Reset</b> — clear all measurements\n• <b>Share</b> — share the average position via SMS, email, etc.\n\n<b>5. The map</b>\n• Red circles = individual measurements\n• Blue circle + marker = average position\n• Crosshair button (top): toggle map following on/off\n• +/- buttons: zoom in/out\n\n<b>6. Settings</b>\nIn the menu → Settings you can change:\n• Number of positions per run\n• Delay between measurements\n• Coordinate format (DM, DD or DMS)\n• Map type (Google Maps or OpenStreetMap)\n\n<b>Tips:</b>\n• Stand still during measurement for best results\n• Run multiple times — more measurements = better average\n• Use satellite map to see exactly where to place the cache</string>
    <string name="about_button_return">Back</string>
    <string name="about_textview_body">Geocache Placer is a tool to help Geocachers get an accurate position for the Geocache they want to place.\n\nPress \"Run\" a few times until the deviation coordinates are close to 0.0000. The app is free and supported by ads.\n\nDeveloped by Rocologo@hotmail.com</string>
